{"seq":31,"at":"2026-10-22","kind":"printed","target":{"type":"wording","id":"w24735"},"reason":"Printed on publish-or-perish card pp-058, category 2; the card's own words are kept in cardText — \"[Physiology and Anatomy] What is the main structural molecule in hair and nails?\nA. Elastin B. Keratin C. Collagen\nAnswer: B. Keratin is the main structural protein found in hair and nails. It’s a fibrous protein that provides strength and resilience to these structures, making them tough and resistant to damage.\".","by":"merge art/architecture, art/design, art/painting, art/sculpture, belief/philosophy, belief/religion, belief/symbols, ear","ref":"quiz-archive/transcripts/publish-or-perish/pp-058.json","changes":[{"field":"en","new":"Which fibrous structural protein is the main material of hair and nails?"},{"field":"de","new":"Welches faserige Strukturprotein ist der Hauptbestandteil von Haaren und Nägeln?"},{"field":"origin","new":"printed"},{"field":"printed","new":{"source":"publish-or-perish","card":"pp-058","category":2}},{"field":"cardText","diff":[["+","[Physiology and Anatomy] What is the main structural molecule in hair and nails?\nA. Elastin B. Keratin C. Collagen\nAnswer: B. Keratin is the main structural protein found in hair and nails. It’s a fibrous protein that provides strength and resilience to these structures, making them tough and resistant to damage."]]},{"field":"fact","new":"f02984"}],"hash":"3094df3d9f34"},
